  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S.Pushpanathan vs The Commissioner Food Safety & ... on 9 March, 2023 Author: M.Dhandapani Bench: M.Dhandapani W.P In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 09.03.2023 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Dhandapani W.P.No.7190 of 2023 and WMP.No.7250 of 2023 S.Pushpanathan ...Petitioner Vs. 1. The Commissioner Food Safety & Standards, Food Business Licensing & Registration Regulation, Chennai - 600 006. 2. The Designation Officer, Department of Food Safety & Drug Administration, Salem District. 3. The Inspector of Police, Kannankurichi Police Station, Salem District. ...Respondents Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus calling for the records of respondent in Na.Ka.No.2697/A1/VuPaThaSa/2022-23 dated 26.12.2022 and quash the same. For Petitioner : Mr.B.Gopalakrishnan For Respondents : Mr.E.Veda Bagath Singh, Spl.GP 1/7 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis S.Pushpanathan vs The Commissioner Food Safety & ... on 9 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179044169/ 1 Order",
    "facts": "The petitioner has filed this writ petition seeking issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the records of the 2nd respondent in respect of the proceedings bearing Na.Ka.No.2697/A1/VuPaThaSa/2022-23 dated 26.12.2022 and quash the same. 3. The case of the petitioner is that the petitioner is running a provisional store in the name and style of \"Omsakthi Maligai\" for the past several years without any violation. While so, on 16.12.2022, the 3rd respondent has registered a false case against the petitioner in Crime No.952 /2022 for the offences under Section 77 of the Juvenile Justice (Care & Protection of Children)Act 2015 and Section 6(a), 6(b) & 24(1) of Cigarette & other Tobacco products Act 2003 on the ground that the petitioner was in https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis possession and selling banned Hannes and Cool Lips to the students. Thereafter, the 2nd respondent passed the present impugned order dated 26.12.2022 bearing Na.Ka.No.2697/A1/VuPaThaSa/2022-23, without affording an opportunity to the petitioner to canvass his grievances and subsequently sealed the petitioner's shop. Aggrieved by the above said order, the petitioner preferred an appeal before the 1st respondent. however, till date no orders have been passed on the same. Hence, the petitioner has came up with this Writ petition challenging the order of the 2nd respondent dated 26.12.2022. 4.",
